Subject: [PATCH] wave: close AP VLAN dependents before parent deletion

Mirror mac80211's ndo_stop ordering: RTNL protects the dependent interface
list while dev_close() sends notifications without the wiphy mutex held.
The later cfg80211 deletion callback can then unregister down children
without recursively taking the wiphy mutex in NETDEV_GOING_DOWN.
Retain child objects; existing BSS/station owners still retire bindings.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/mtlk_df_user.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/mtlk_df_user.c
@@ -2211,8 +2211,18 @@
 {
   mtlk_hw_t *hw;
   mtlk_df_user_t* df_user =  mtlk_df_user_from_ndev(ndev);
+  struct wave_ap_vlan *vlan, *next;
 
   MTLK_CHECK_DF_USER(df_user);
+
+  /* Like mac80211, close dependent ports from ndo_stop under RTNL, before
+   * the parent's locked cfg80211 deletion callback. Their close notifiers
+   * acquire the wiphy mutex; unregistering an UP child there would recurse.
+   * Close only the ports; existing BSS/STA owners retire their bindings.
+   */
+  ASSERT_RTNL();
+  list_for_each_entry_safe(vlan, next, &df_user->ap_vlans, node)
+    dev_close(vlan->wdev.netdev);
 
   ILOG0_SS("%s, %s: stop the interface", current->comm, mtlk_df_user_get_name(df_user));
   wave_df_tx_queue_stop(df_user);
